{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE SITE FOOTER — HomePageV3.dc.html's footer, on every shell page
  Phase 4 (§8.1 item 9: "the codebase footer, restyled as in the DC")
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The site's only footer, mounted by `layout/shell.twig` inside the scroller after the
  page, so it is reached by scrolling and never pinned. Written from the DC; the rules
  below are the destroyed `layout/footer.twig`'s, carried because its inventory marks
  them MUST RESTORE (docs/handoff/inventory/_partials.md):

  · It is the only every-page link to /refunds, /vendor-terms, /support, /philosophy,
    /challenges and /newsletter, the legal row, and the /org front door a partner
    arrives at cold. Three of those (Challenges, Our philosophy, Newsletter) are not in
    the DC's columns and are added at the end of the column they belong to — a page
    nothing links is a page nobody finds (`PublicIaTest`). Deviation, PHASE-4.md.
  · "Live in …" is `nations_live()`, counted from the awards — NEVER typed. The sentence
    was typed into this footer once and was wrong the day a second nation went live.
    "Building toward" is the operator's ambition setting, `nations_count`: two claims.
  · Activity is gone (§8.23: the timeline is Discover's Live tab now).
  · Cookies re-opens the consent choices in place (`data-ag-do="consent-open"`, bound by
    consent.js) and is a plain link to /cookies#choices without script — the way back to
    the choices at ≥600px that Phase 2 left waiting for this footer (GAPS §8c item 10).
  · Social links open a new tab and say so in their names.

  No capitals: the DC's column titles are 11px uppercase tracked; here they are sentence
  case at 12.5 (§6.2, owner Q4/Q5). Every link is a literal `href` in the markup, so the
  sweeps that ask "is this page linked from anywhere" (PublicIaTest) can read it. The DC's #0c2225 is not a palette colour; the band is
  `--ag-ink`, and its words are `--ag-surface` mixed toward the ink (Accent: `surface` is
  the word on ink).
#}
